WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
In South Cambridgeshire, a new
town is planned in the fields.

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:09.610
Northstowe is planned to have 10,000
homes and about 25,000 people.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.750
The Outer Hebrides, off
north-west Scotland,

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.030
lost people between the
2011 and 2022 censuses:

5
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.510
the biggest fall of any
Scottish council area.

6
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.430
There, 13.7 per cent of people are
aged 55 or over and living alone,

7
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.630
the highest share in Scotland.

8
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.630
So why are some villages
booming while others empty?

9
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.670
Better weather?

10
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.810
Newer houses?

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.170
Lost farms?

12
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.490
In this mission, you'll compare one rural
area that is growing with one that is

13
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.750
in decline.

14
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.350
Then you'll explore how each
change reshapes schools,

15
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.130
shops and jobs.

16
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.430
Your mission: explain why some UK
villages grow while others lose people.
